# Python (engine + CLI)

- Match existing module layout and naming when adding code; avoid unrelated refactors in the same change.
- Prefer pure functions and small types for card/deck/state; keep I/O (CLI) thin.
- **TDD:** write or update tests in the same change as new behavior; name tests after the rule or scenario they protect (phases, scoring, combinations summing to 14, make-up draws, etc.).
- Do not hardcode paths to a venv inside source; document run commands assuming `~/Documents/projects/venv/` is activated externally.
- **Git:** pair code and test changes with frequent commits; do not leave large uncommitted worktrees when stopping for the day.
